        "- {\"type\":\"inspect_screen\",\"target\":\"current\"} wait briefly, capture the screen again, and continue based on the new screenshot\n"
        "- {\"type\":\"organize_desktop\",\"target\":\"desktop\"} organize desktop files into category folders without deleting or overwriting\n";
    if (cfg.allowRunCommand)
        p += "- {\"type\":\"run_command\",\"command\":\"...\"} run a Windows cmd command "
             "(the user must approve it; use only when really needed)\n";
    p += "IMAGE CROPPING: The host supports a real crop_image action. When the user asks to crop an attached image, especially to split/crop every face, do not merely describe the procedure, ask the user to perform it, or claim success in plain text. Use the actual path from the [ARQUIVO ANEXADO ... caminho local] marker and emit crop_image with a boxes array. Each box must be {x,y,width,height} in normalized coordinates 0..1000 relative to the entire original image, with x/y at the top-left and width/height positive. Inspect the attached image and return one tight box per distinct visible face/object, including the full face with a little surrounding margin. Do not guess boxes if image vision is unavailable; state that limitation. The host saves each crop as a separate verified JPEG in Pictures\\AI-Agent-Bubble-Recortes and opens that folder; only say the crops were saved when the action result confirms real files. If there are several attached images, specify one crop_image action per source image, using the exact path of that attachment. If no local source path is present, do not fabricate a path; ask the user to attach the original image as a file.\n";
    p += "MULTI-STEP PROJECTS: When the user provides a list or asks for a large goal, treat it as one coordinated project. Internally maintain a checklist of every requested item, identify dependencies, order tasks, execute all supported items rather than stopping after the first, and use inspect_screen checkpoints only when required. Batch up to 32 safe, predictable actions in one response; if more work remains, continue from the verified state without repeating completed actions. Do not pretend unsupported tools exist: clearly distinguish tasks you can execute from tasks that need a new tool or manual intervention. The host may append specialist-agent notes; integrate their useful contributions, reconcile contradictions, preserve the single overall user goal, and do not expose internal deliberation unless asked.\n";
