         "The host selects a vision-capable model when appropriate and handles provider compatibility. "
         "If you cannot interpret an image, report that limitation and do not invent screen details. "
         "VISUAL HONESTY: for wallpaper or image descriptions, ground every claim in visible evidence. Do not default to generic descriptions such as black backgrounds, stars, geometric patterns, or colors unless they are actually visible. If the user challenges your description (for example, asks 'tem certeza?' or says it is wrong) and a new image is attached, re-examine that image independently; do not defend your previous answer merely for consistency and do not simply agree with the user. If the image does not support a confident description, explicitly say what is uncertain. The current image outranks guesses in the conversation history. "
         "An image-capability error may trigger another configured compatible vision model only when "
         "fallback is enabled or the user has explicitly consented. If website automation only opens search results/templates without creating the "
         "requested design, use create_presentation as a fallback and do not claim the website "
         "itself was edited. Preserve context in follow-ups. If the user asks to show/open/view "
         "a slide or presentation you generated, use open_latest_presentation and open the actual "
         ".pptx rather than a generic folder. Do not repeat searches or open tabs unless asked. "
         "When screen vision is on, use the provided screenshot to ground mouse actions. Coordinates x,y,x2,y2 are normalized integers from 0 to 1000 on the full screenshot: (0,0) is the top-left and (1000,1000) the bottom-right; do not use physical pixels. For a visually identified item, click its center, not its border. You can move the cursor first, but click is the action that activates it. BATCH safe, predictable actions in one actions array instead of asking the host to call you after every click. Use inspect_screen only at meaningful checkpoints where the UI probably changed (for example, after opening a context menu, navigating to another page, opening a dialog, or applying a setting); never request a fresh screenshot after a simple cursor move, and avoid repeated inspection when the previous screenshot is still valid. Each inspect_screen creates another model request, so conserve calls. For forms, first click the visible field, then use type_text or key; use CTRL+L for browser address bar, ENTER to submit, CTRL+R to reload, CTRL+W to close a tab. Never claim a click succeeded merely because it was sent; inspect the next screenshot at the next meaningful checkpoint. Do not click destructive controls, purchase/checkout, send/post/publish buttons, grant permissions, or delete files without an explicit user confirmation. Do not automate CAPTCHA solving or enter passwords; ask the user to handle login and sensitive steps. If no screenshot is attached, do not guess coordinates; ask the user to enable screen vision or send a screenshot. Only claim success based on action results. An ask_user confirmation is NOT proof that the requested task succeeded; verify the actual result via a screenshot or a concrete API/file check. If unverified, explicitly say so and do not write success language to the history. A screenshot of a Pinterest result is not a downloaded image and is not sufficient to claim a wallpaper was applied. Desktop organization moves recognized file "
         "types and never overwrites. Window control requires a listed verb and visible title. "
         "IMPORTANT DISTINCTION: a wallpaper/background image being rotated is NOT the same as the entire display being rotated. Never send CTRL+ALT+UP or another display-orientation shortcut for a wallpaper request. For an explicit request to rotate the wallpaper image, use wallpaper_rotate. If the user only reports that the wallpaper looks rotated without asking you to change it, ask whether they want to rotate the image or change the display orientation. For minimizing all open windows, use WIN+M (not WIN+D, because WIN+D toggles Show Desktop). Do not treat browser tabs as separate windows. "
         "Return a JSON mood field alongside reply/actions, one of idle, happy, curious, confused, sad, surprised, or error, chosen to fit the conversational tone. The mod uses matching files from the configured avatar folder; do not mention unsupported avatar states. Answer in the user's language and keep replies concise. CRITICAL RESPONSE TIMING: if actions are included, do not narrate the plan in reply; set reply to an empty string or a very short neutral value because the host executes the entire action batch before speaking. Never write future-tense progress narration such as 'vou clicar', 'agora vou', 'estou abrindo' when actions are pending. After a visual continuation, if no more actions are needed, give ONE very short, natural final sentence (usually 3–8 words), in past tense. Do not narrate the action list, implementation details, keyboard shortcuts, internal status notes, temporary file paths, or explain routine successful steps. For success, prefer a natural confirmation such as **Pronto! O papel de parede foi girado.** Use Markdown bold for the key confirmation phrase; never include paths unless the user asks. Mention a failure briefly and honestly if a step failed or remains unverified. Do not claim overall success just because an input was sent. If a workflow needs multiple UI changes, return the largest safe batch possible and add inspect_screen only at necessary checkpoints. If the API reports quota/rate-limit errors, stop instead of retrying repeatedly. If login, CAPTCHA, verification, "
         "permission, or another manual step is needed, use ask_user to pause and request it; "
         "never bypass authentication or claim completion before the task is actually done. When "
         "a screenshot shows a login/CAPTCHA/permission dialog, ask the user to intervene and "
         "wait. For voice changes, use voice_control; for skipping/advancing songs, use "
         "media_control next; pause/resume uses play_pause; volume requests use volume_control. "
         "Do not claim an action is impossible when a supported action exists. Voice selection "
         "depends on compatible voices installed in Windows.\n";
    p += "File attachment rules: text/code files are supplied as extracted text and images as image input when the chosen model supports vision. For binary formats that the host cannot extract, you may receive only filename, MIME type, and file size; never claim to have read their contents unless the actual content is present. Very large inputs may still exceed a provider's context window. When asked to create or edit this mod's source, return the complete source in a fenced code block when practical, not merely a patch fragment. Never overwrite source automatically from an AI reply. Source replacement is handled locally only after the user explicitly requests it, a source path is configured, a backup is created, and the user confirms. Never claim the result compiles; the user must compile and test in Windhawk.\n";
    if (!cfg.extraInstructions.empty())
        p += "Extra instructions from the user: " + ToUtf8(cfg.extraInstructions) + "\n";
    if (!apps.empty()) {
        std::string list;
        int count = 0;
        for (const auto& a : apps) {
            std::string n = ToUtf8(a.name);
            if (list.size() + n.size() > 3500 || count >= 160) break;
            if (!list.empty()) list += "; ";
            list += n;
            ++count;
        }
        p += "Installed apps (Start menu): " + list + "\n";
    }
    return p;
}

struct Request {
    std::wstring url;
    std::wstring headers;
    std::string body;
    std::wstring error;
};

Request BuildRequest(const Settings& cfg, const std::string& system,
                     const std::vector<Msg>& hist) {
    Request r;
    std::wstring base = EffectiveBase(cfg);
    std::string model = ToUtf8(EffectiveModel(cfg));
    if (base.empty()) {
        r.error = L"Configure a URL base do provedor personalizado.";
        return r;
    }
    if (model.empty()) {
        r.error = L"Informe o nome do modelo nas configurações.";
        return r;
    }
    r.headers = L"Content-Type: application/json\r\nAccept: application/json\r\n";

    if (cfg.provider == Provider::Gemini) {
        r.url = base + L"/models/" + FromUtf8(model) + L":generateContent";
        r.headers += L"x-goog-api-key: " + cfg.apiKey + L"\r\n";
        std::string b = "{\"systemInstruction\":{\"parts\":[{\"text\":" + JStr(system) +
                        "}]},\"contents\":[";
        for (size_t i = 0; i < hist.size(); ++i) {
            if (i) b += ",";
            b += std::string("{\"role\":\"") + (hist[i].user ? "user" : "model") + "\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":" + JStr(hist[i].text) + "}";
            if (hist[i].user && !hist[i].imageBase64.empty())
                b += ", {\"inline_data\":{\"mime_type\":\"image/jpeg\",\"data\":" + JStr(hist[i].imageBase64) + "}}";
            if (hist[i].user) for (const auto& image : hist[i].attachedImageBase64)
                if (!image.empty()) b += ", {\"inline_data\":{\"mime_type\":\"image/jpeg\",\"data\":" + JStr(image) + "}}";
            b += "]}";
        }
        b += "],\"generationConfig\":{\"temperature\":0.3,\"responseMimeType\":\"application/json\"}}";
        r.body = std::move(b);
    } else if (cfg.provider == Provider::Anthropic) {
        r.url = base + L"/messages";
        r.headers += L"x-api-key: " + cfg.apiKey + L"\r\nanthropic-version: 2023-06-01\r\n";
        std::string b = "{\"model\":" + JStr(model) + ",\"max_tokens\":16384,\"system\":" +
                        JStr(system) + ",\"messages\":[";
        for (size_t i = 0; i < hist.size(); ++i) {
            if (i) b += ",";
            b += std::string("{\"role\":\"") + (hist[i].user ? "user" : "assistant") + "\",\"content\":";
            const bool hasImages = hist[i].user && (!hist[i].imageBase64.empty() || !hist[i].attachedImageBase64.empty());
            if (hasImages) {
                b += "[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":" + JStr(hist[i].text) + "}";
                if (!hist[i].imageBase64.empty()) b += ",{\"type\":\"image\",\"source\":{\"type\":\"base64\",\"media_type\":\"image/jpeg\",\"data\":" + JStr(hist[i].imageBase64) + "}}";
                for (const auto& image : hist[i].attachedImageBase64) if (!image.empty())
                    b += ",{\"type\":\"image\",\"source\":{\"type\":\"base64\",\"media_type\":\"image/jpeg\",\"data\":" + JStr(image) + "}}";
                b += "]";
            } else b += JStr(hist[i].text);
            b += "}";
        }
        b += "]}";
        r.body = std::move(b);
    } else {
        // OpenAI/NVIDIA/Custom: formato compatível com Chat Completions multimodal.
        // NVIDIA hosted API usa uma rota canônica; não derive o endpoint do nome do modelo.
        if (cfg.provider == Provider::Nvidia) {
            r.url = L"https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/chat/completions";
        } else {
            r.url = base;
            constexpr wchar_t kChatPath[] = L"/chat/completions";
            const size_t chatPathLen = sizeof(kChatPath) / sizeof(kChatPath[0]) - 1;
            if (r.url.size() < chatPathLen ||
                r.url.compare(r.url.size() - chatPathLen, chatPathLen, kChatPath) != 0) {
                r.url += kChatPath;
            }
        }
        if (!cfg.apiKey.empty()) r.headers += L"Authorization: Bearer " + cfg.apiKey + L"\r\n";
        std::string b = "{\"model\":" + JStr(model) + ",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":" + JStr(system) + "}";
        for (const auto& m : hist) {
            b += std::string(",{\"role\":\"") + (m.user ? "user" : "assistant") + "\",\"content\":";
            const bool hasImages = m.user && (!m.imageBase64.empty() || !m.attachedImageBase64.empty());
            if (hasImages) {
                b += "[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":" + JStr(m.text) + "}";
                if (!m.imageBase64.empty()) b += ",{\"type\":\"image_url\",\"image_url\":{\"url\":" + JStr("data:image/jpeg;base64," + m.imageBase64) + "}}";
                for (const auto& image : m.attachedImageBase64) if (!image.empty())
                    b += ",{\"type\":\"image_url\",\"image_url\":{\"url\":" + JStr("data:image/jpeg;base64," + image) + "}}";
                b += "]";
            } else b += JStr(m.text);
            b += "}";
        }
        b += "]";
        if (cfg.provider != Provider::OpenAI) b += ",\"temperature\":0.3";
        b += "}";
        r.body = std::move(b);
    }
    return r;
}

std::wstring ErrorMessage(const JV& v) {
    if (const JV* e = v.Get("error")) {
        if (e->type == JV::Str) return FromUtf8(e->s);
        if (const JV* m = e->Get("message")) return FromUtf8(m->AsStr());
    }
    if (const JV* m = v.Get("message")) if (m->type == JV::Str) return FromUtf8(m->s);
    if (const JV* d = v.Get("detail")) {
        if (d->type == JV::Str) return FromUtf8(d->s);
        if (d->type == JV::Arr && d->At(0))
            if (const JV* m = d->At(0)->Get("msg")) return FromUtf8(m->AsStr());
    }
    return L"";
}

bool ExtractReply(Provider p, const std::string& body, std::string& text,
                  std::wstring& err) {
    JV v;
    JsonParser parser(body);
    if (!parser.Parse(v) || v.type != JV::Obj) {
        err = L"Resposta inválida do servidor.";
        return false;
    }
    std::wstring apiErr = ErrorMessage(v);
    if (!apiErr.empty()) {
        err = apiErr;
        return false;
    }
    if (p == Provider::Gemini) {
        if (const JV* c = v.Get("candidates"))
            if (const JV* c0 = c->At(0))
                if (const JV* content = c0->Get("content"))
                    if (const JV* parts = content->Get("parts"))
                        for (const auto& part : parts->arr)
                            if (const JV* t = part.Get("text")) text += t->AsStr();
        if (text.empty()) {
            const JV* fb = v.Get("promptFeedback");
            const JV* br = fb ? fb->Get("blockReason") : nullptr;
            err = br ? L"Pedido bloqueado pelo Gemini: " + FromUtf8(br->AsStr())
                     : L"O Gemini não retornou texto.";
            return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
    if (p == Provider::Anthropic) {
        if (const JV* c = v.Get("content"))
            for (const auto& block : c->arr)
                if (const JV* t = block.Get("text")) text += t->AsStr();
        if (text.empty()) {
            err = L"O Claude não retornou texto.";
            return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
    if (const JV* ch = v.Get("choices"))
        if (const JV* c0 = ch->At(0))
            if (const JV* msg = c0->Get("message"))
                if (const JV* content = msg->Get("content")) {
                    if (content->type == JV::Str) {
                        text = content->s;
                    } else if (content->type == JV::Arr) {
                        for (const auto& part : content->arr)
                            if (const JV* t = part.Get("text")) text += t->AsStr();
                    }
                }
    if (text.empty()) {
        err = L"O modelo não retornou texto.";
        return false;
    }
    return true;
}

// Rejeita respostas de metadados/safety ou texto livre que não contenha o JSON
// obrigatório do agente. Isso permite ao AiThread tentar outro provedor configurado.
bool HasExpectedAgentPayload(const std::string& raw) {
    const size_t a = raw.find('{');
    const size_t b = raw.rfind('}');
    if (a == std::string::npos || b == std::string::npos || b <= a) return false;
    const std::string json = raw.substr(a, b - a + 1);
    JV v;
    JsonParser parser(json);
    if (!parser.Parse(v) || v.type != JV::Obj) return false;
    const JV* reply = v.Get("reply");
    const JV* actions = v.Get("actions");
    // Alguns modelos/provedores podem devolver metadados como "User Safety: safe"
    // em vez de responder ao usuário. Não exponha isso como conversa normal.
    if (reply && reply->type == JV::Str) {
        std::string lower = reply->s;
        for (char& ch : lower) {
            if (ch >= 'A' && ch <= 'Z') ch = static_cast<char>(ch - 'A' + 'a');
        }
        const bool safetyLabel = lower.find("user safety:") != std::string::npos ||
                                 lower.find("assistant safety:") != std::string::npos ||
                                 lower.find("safety classification:") != std::string::npos;
        const bool hasActions = actions && actions->type == JV::Arr && !actions->arr.empty();
        if (safetyLabel && !hasActions) return false;
    }
    return reply != nullptr || actions != nullptr;
}

// Detect a frequent multimodal failure mode: the model returns a normal-looking
// JSON payload but claims it cannot see the screen even though an image was sent.
// Such a response is not accepted as a valid visual analysis; AiThread can try
// another configured vision-capable provider instead.
bool IsVisionAccessDenialPayload(const std::string& raw) {
    std::wstring visibleText;
    JV v;
    std::string candidate = raw;
    size_t open = candidate.find('{');
    size_t close = candidate.rfind('}');
    if (open != std::string::npos && close != std::string::npos && close > open)
        candidate = candidate.substr(open, close - open + 1);
    JsonParser parser(candidate);
    if (parser.Parse(v) && v.type == JV::Obj) {
        const JV* reply = v.Get("reply");
        if (reply && reply->type == JV::Str) visibleText = FromUtf8(reply->s);
    }
    // Providers sometimes omit the agent's JSON wrapper (e.g. a raw denial
    // or a safety message). Inspect plain text too, but never treat it as analysis.
    if (visibleText.empty()) visibleText = FromUtf8(raw);
    const std::wstring t = Lower(Trim(visibleText));
    static const wchar_t* phrases[] = {
        L"não tenho acesso à sua área de trabalho", L"nao tenho acesso a sua area de trabalho",
        L"não tenho acesso à área de trabalho", L"nao tenho acesso a area de trabalho",
        L"não consigo ver sua área de trabalho", L"nao consigo ver sua area de trabalho",
        L"não tenho acesso à tela", L"nao tenho acesso a tela",
        L"não consigo ver sua tela", L"nao consigo ver sua tela",
        L"não consigo ver a tela", L"nao consigo ver a tela",
        L"não posso ver sua tela", L"nao posso ver sua tela",
        L"não consigo visualizar a tela", L"nao consigo visualizar a tela",
        L"envie uma captura de tela", L"envie uma captura", L"mande uma captura de tela",
        L"i cannot see your screen", L"i can't see your screen", L"i cannot view your screen",
        L"i can't view your screen", L"i cannot access your desktop", L"i can't access your desktop",
        L"i don't have access to your desktop", L"i do not have access to your screen",
        L"i cannot see the image", L"i can't see the image", L"i can't view screenshots",
        L"please send me a screenshot", L"upload a screenshot", L"provide a screenshot"
    };
    for (const auto* phrase : phrases) if (t.find(phrase) != std::wstring::npos) return true;
    return false;
}

// Only reject models known to be text-only. Unknown/custom IDs are allowed to
// make one real request because providers frequently expose their own multimodal
// model names; an API rejection then becomes a normal fallback candidate failure.
bool IsImageCapabilityError(const std::wstring& raw) {
    const std::wstring e = Lower(raw);
    static const wchar_t* terms[] = {
        L"does not support image", L"doesn't support image", L"image input is not supported",
        L"image_url is not supported", L"unsupported image input", L"image modality is not supported",
        L"multimodal input is not supported", L"vision is not supported", L"text-only model",
        L"only accepts text", L"não aceita imagens", L"nao aceita imagens",
        L"não suporta imagem", L"nao suporta imagem", L"somente texto", L"apenas texto",
        L"modelo não oferece visão", L"modelo nao oferece visao"
    };
    for (const auto* term : terms) if (e.find(term) != std::wstring::npos) return true;
    return false;
}

bool IsKnownTextOnlyModel(const Settings& cfg) {
    std::wstring m = Lower(Trim(cfg.model));
    std::wstring base = Lower(Trim(cfg.customBase));
    if (m.empty()) m = Lower(InfoFor(cfg.provider).defaultModel);
    if (m.find(L"embedding") != std::wstring::npos ||
        m.find(L"text-embedding") != std::wstring::npos ||
        m.find(L"whisper") != std::wstring::npos ||
        m.find(L"-tts") != std::wstring::npos ||
        m.find(L"transcribe") != std::wstring::npos ||
        m.find(L"moderation") != std::wstring::npos ||
        m.find(L"gpt-oss") != std::wstring::npos) return true;
    if ((cfg.provider == Provider::Custom || cfg.provider == Provider::Nvidia) &&
        m.find(L"llama-3.1") != std::wstring::npos &&
        m.find(L"vision") == std::wstring::npos) return true;
    if (cfg.provider == Provider::Custom && base.find(L"api.groq.com") != std::wstring::npos &&
        m.find(L"vision") == std::wstring::npos &&
        m.find(L"llama-4-scout") == std::wstring::npos &&
        m.find(L"llama-4-maverick") == std::wstring::npos &&
        m.find(L"qwen2.5-vl") == std::wstring::npos) {
        // The default Groq model configured by this mod is text-only.
        if (m == L"openai/gpt-oss-120b") return true;
    }
    return false;
}

